    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Team Paul Reddy is delighted to bring to the market No. 133 Riverside Park, an impressive and substantially renovated three-bedroom, three-bathroom semi-detached family home extending to approximately 175 sq.m. This exceptional property combines generous living accommodation with a high-quality modern finish and benefits from a large two-storey rear extension and an attic study/storage room with planning permission, a large driveway, a landscaped low-maintenance rear garden and a substantial concrete outbuilding with power and plumbing. The property has been rewired and re-plumbed as part of its extensive renovation and further features a modern fully integrated kitchen with recessed lighting and large island, wood panelling throughout, spacious open-plan kitchen/living/dining area, separate sitting room, utility room, guest W.C. with shower and an impressive master bedroom with large walk-in wardrobe and en-suite, double-glazed windows and gas-fired central heating. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation has been thoughtfully designed to provide exceptional modern family living. The ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hall leading into the impressive open-plan kitchen, living and dining area, which forms the heart of the home. The contemporary kitchen is fully integrated and features a large central island, recessed lighting and excellent storage, while large sliding doors provide a seamless connection to the landscaped rear garden. The property also benefits from a separate sitting room, utility room and guest W.C. incorporating a shower.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, together with the main family bathroom. The generous master bedroom is particularly impressive, featuring a large walk-in wardrobe and en-suite bathroom. The additional bedrooms provide excellent accommodation for family members or guests. The property also benefits from an attic study/storage room, providing valuable additional space that can be used as a home office, study, hobby room, or storage area.\r\n\r\nTo the front, the property benefits from a driveway providing extensive off-street parking. The rear garden is a particular highlight, enjoying an east/south-facing aspect and having been thoughtfully landscaped to create an attractive, private and low-maintenance outdoor space. The rear garden is further enhanced by a substantial concrete outbuilding, thoughtfully divided into three separate sections comprising a storage area, playroom and bathroom. The building benefits from both power and plumbing, offering excellent versatility and a range of potential uses, subject to the purchaser’s requirements. A roller shutter door provides convenient access, including to the BBQ area, while the additional bathroom and generous internal space make this a particularly useful feature of the property. Whether used for storage, children’s play, hobbies, a home workshop or additional recreational space, this excellent ancillary building provides a valuable extension of the home’s overall living and lifestyle offering.\r\n\r\nNo. 133 Riverside Park represents a rare opportunity to acquire a large, substantially renovated and stylish family home offering generous accommodation and excellent outdoor space."
      },
